 3475                     ;
 3476                     ; MOST FUNCTIONS TAKE A SINGLE ARGUMENT.
 3477                     ; THE RETURN ADDRESS OF THESE FUNCTIONS IS "CHKNUM"
 3478                     ; WHICH ASCERTAINS THAT [VALTYP]=0  (NUMERIC).
 3479                     ; NORMAL FUNCTIONS THAT RETURN STRING RESULTS
 3480                     ; (E.G., CHR$) MUST POP OFF THAT RETURN ADDR AND
 3481                     ; RETURN DIRECTLY TO "FRMEVL".
 3482                     ;
 3483                     ; THE SO-CALLED "FUNNY" FUNCTIONS CAN TAKE MORE THAN ONE ARGUMENT,
 3484                     ; THE FIRST OF WHICH MUST BE STRING AND THE SECOND OF WHICH
 3485                     ; MUST BE A NUMBER BETWEEN 0 AND 255.
 3486                     ; THE CLOSED PARENTHESIS MUST BE CHECKED AND RETURN IS DIRECTLY
 3487                     ; TO "FRMEVL" WITH THE TEXT PNTR POINTING BEYOND THE ")".
 3488                     ; THE POINTER TO THE DESCRIPTOR OF THE STRING ARGUMENT
 3489                     ; IS STORED ON THE STACK UNDERNEATH THE VALUE OF THE
 3490                     ; INTEGER ARGUMENT.
